diff --git a/board/cargt/imx93_00363/README.ddr-timing b/board/cargt/imx93_00363/README.ddr-timing
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..4f6391f3ca4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/board/cargt/imx93_00363/README.ddr-timing
@@ -0,0 +1,202 @@
+LPDDR4X DDR Timing Selection — Cargt i.MX93 00363 SOM
+======================================================
+
+Overview
+--------
+The SPL reads a Cargt EEPROM on lpi2c1 (i2c@44340000) to determine the
+installed LPDDR4X part parameters, then selects the matching pre-generated
+timing structure before calling ddr_init().
+
+Three Kconfig options control which selection method is compiled in:
+
+  CONFIG_CARGT_IMX93_00363_LPDDR4X_TIMING_BY_EEPROM   (production default)
+  CONFIG_CARGT_IMX93_00363_LPDDR4X_TIMING_BY_BOARD_ID (GPIO-based)
+  CONFIG_CARGT_IMX93_00363_LPDDR4X_TIMING_BY_NAME     (filename override)
+
+
+Supported Variants
+------------------
+Each combination of (size, speed, rank) has its own timing file:
+
+  Size    Speed       Rank   Source file                              Status
+  ------  ----------  -----  ---------------------------------------  ----------------------------
+  512 MB  3200 MT/s   1      cargt_lpddr4x_512mb_3200mts_timing.c    DDR training verified (1)
+  512 MB  3733 MT/s   1      cargt_lpddr4x_512mb_3733mts_timing.c    Structurally correct (1)
+  1 GB    3200 MT/s   1      cargt_lpddr4x_1gbyte_3200mts_timing.c   Full boot verified
+  1 GB    3733 MT/s   1      cargt_lpddr4x_1gbyte_3733mts_timing.c   Full boot verified
+  2 GB    3200 MT/s   1      cargt_lpddr4x_2gbyte_3200mts_timing.c   Full boot verified (2)
+  2 GB    3733 MT/s   1      cargt_lpddr4x_2gbyte_3733mts_timing.c   Full boot verified (2)
+  2 GB    3200 MT/s   2      cargt_lpddr4x_2gbyte_3200mts_timing.c   Full boot verified
+  2 GB    3733 MT/s   2      cargt_lpddr4x_2gbyte_3733mts_timing.c   Full boot verified
+
+Note 1: 512 MB variants cannot be fully validated on the imx93-cargt-00363-00365
+machine because that machine requires >=1 GB DDR (CARGT_EEPROM_DRAM_START would
+fall outside the 512 MB DDRC window, and the PHY training parameters were
+generated for a specific 512 MB die).  Both variants need a true 512 MB part for
+full boot confirmation.  512 MB support is planned for the headless / i.MX91
+machine variant.
+
+Note 2: The 2 GB timing files each contain two `dram_timing_info` structs: the
+main rank2 struct (cargt_lpddr4x_2gbyte_3xxx mts_timing) and a rank1 variant
+(cargt_lpddr4x_2gbyte_3xxxmts_rank1_timing).  The rank1 struct shares the
+expensive static ddrphy_cfg and phy_pie arrays with the rank2 struct to keep SPL
+SRAM usage within budget; only the DDRC cfg, per-FSP DDRC timing registers and
+PHY message blocks differ (rank1: CS1 disabled, MR11 ODT=0x46 vs 0x26).
+
+
+SPL Boot Flow (EEPROM mode)
+---------------------------
+ROM → SPL entry
+  1. ddr_init() is NOT yet called
+  2. PMIC configured, I2C bus ready
+  3. cargt_eeprom_read()  — reads 256-byte EEPROM at i2c@44340000 / 0x50
+  4. cargt_eeprom_get_dram_size_mb()   → dram_size_mbytes
+     cargt_eeprom_get_dram_speed_mts() → dram_speed_mts
+     cargt_eeprom_get_dram_rank()       → dram_rank
+  5. Minimum RAM check (if CONFIG_CARGT_IMX93_00363_MIN_SDRAM_SIZE_MB > 0):
+       if dram_size_mbytes < minimum → override to failsafe 1GB/3200/rank1
+       and print a WARNING (does NOT hang; board stays bootable)
+  6. select_dram_timing(speed, size, rank) → struct dram_timing_info *
+  7. rank-2 patch: if rank==2 && size>1024, adjust DDRC CS1 BNDS
+  8. ddr_init(ptiming)
+  9. gd->bd->bi_dram[0].size = dram_size_mbytes * SZ_1M
+ 10. SPL continues → loads imx-boot container from eMMC / USB SDP
+
+
+Minimum RAM Enforcement
+-----------------------
+Defined in board/cargt/imx93_00363/Kconfig:
+
+  config CARGT_IMX93_00363_MIN_SDRAM_SIZE_MB
+      int "Minimum required SDRAM size in MB (0 = no minimum)"
+      default 0
+
+Machine defconfigs set this to reflect their DTS reserved-memory layout:
+
+  imx93-cargt-00363-00365_defconfig    : CONFIG_CARGT_IMX93_00363_MIN_SDRAM_SIZE_MB=1024
+  imx93-cargt-00363-osm-som_defconfig  : CONFIG_CARGT_IMX93_00363_MIN_SDRAM_SIZE_MB=1024
+
+A headless or 512 MB machine should leave the default (0) or set it to 512.
+
+Failsafe: on an out-of-range EEPROM value the SPL falls back to 1 GB /
+3200 MT/s / rank1 rather than halting, allowing the board to boot and the
+EEPROM to be corrected in U-Boot proper.
+
+
+File Layout
+-----------
+board/cargt/imx93_00363/
+  cargt_lpddr4x_<size>_<speed>mts_timing.c   One file per variant (see table)
+  cargt_lpddr4x_timing_shared.c/.h            Shared FSP1/FSP2 message blocks
+                                               and ddr_phy_pie[] (not used by
+                                               current variants — each file uses
+                                               a local PIE via include/)
+  cargt_lpddr4x_fsp0_cfg_shared.c             Shared FSP0 1D message block
+                                               (legacy; current variant files
+                                               declare their own local copy)
+  cargt_lpddr4x_3200mts_csr.c/.h             Trained CSR array + count macro
+  cargt_lpddr4x_3733mts_csr.c/.h               for 3200 MT/s and 3733 MT/s
+  spl-cargt.c                                 EEPROM read, timing dispatch,
+                                               rank-2 patch, ddr_init call
+  include/
+    ddrc_cfg_<variant>_elements.inc           DDRC controller registers
+    ddrphy_cfg_<variant>_elements.inc         PHY initialisation registers
+    dram_fsp_cfg_<variant>_elements.inc       Per-FSP DDRC timing (dram_fsp_cfg)
+    fsp0_cfg_<variant>_elements.inc           P0 1D training message block
+    fsp1_cfg_<variant>_elements.inc           P1 1D training message block
+    fsp2_cfg_<variant>_elements.inc           P2 1D training message block
+    fsp0_2d_cfg_<variant>_elements.inc        P0 2D training message block
+    phy_pie_<variant>_elements.inc            PHY init engine (PIE) program
+  generated_timings_for_reference/
+    lpddr4x_<variant>_generated.c            Original DDR Tool output; source
+                                               of truth for all inc file data
+
+
+Timing File Structure
+---------------------
+Each cargt_lpddr4x_*_timing.c follows this pattern:
+
+  #include "cargt_lpddr4x_timing_shared.h"
+  #include "cargt_lpddr4x_<speed>mts_csr.h"
+
+  static struct dram_cfg_param ddr_ddrc_cfg[]          = { #include "include/ddrc_cfg_<v>.inc"       };
+  static struct dram_cfg_param ddr_fsp0_cfg_<v>[]      = { #include "include/fsp0_cfg_<v>.inc"      };
+  static struct dram_cfg_param ddr_fsp1_cfg_<v>[]      = { #include "include/fsp1_cfg_<v>.inc"      };
+  static struct dram_cfg_param ddr_fsp2_cfg_<v>[]      = { #include "include/fsp2_cfg_<v>.inc"      };
+  static struct dram_cfg_param ddr_fsp0_2d_cfg_<v>[]   = { #include "include/fsp0_2d_cfg_<v>.inc"   };
+  static struct dram_cfg_param ddr_phy_pie_<v>[]       = { #include "include/phy_pie_<v>.inc"       };
+  static struct dram_cfg_param ddr_ddrphy_cfg[]        = { #include "include/ddrphy_cfg_<v>.inc"    };
+  static struct dram_fsp_cfg  ddr_dram_fsp_cfg[]       = { #include "include/dram_fsp_cfg_<v>.inc"  };
+
+  struct dram_timing_info cargt_lpddr4x_<variant>_timing = {
+      .ddrc_cfg_num           = ARRAY_SIZE(ddr_ddrc_cfg),
+      .ddrphy_trained_csr     = ddr_lpddr4x_<speed>mts_trained_csr,
+      .ddrphy_trained_csr_num = DDR_LPDDR4X_<SPEED>MTS_TRAINED_CSR_NUM,
+      .ddrphy_pie             = ddr_phy_pie_<v>,
+      .ddrphy_pie_num         = ARRAY_SIZE(ddr_phy_pie_<v>),
+      ...
+  };
+
+Rules:
+  - All local arrays use ARRAY_SIZE() for their counts.
+  - DDR_FSP1_CFG_NUM / DDR_FSP2_CFG_NUM are used only if shared extern arrays
+    are referenced (avoid — prefer local arrays with ARRAY_SIZE).
+  - FSP0 array names must be unique per variant (e.g. ddr_fsp0_cfg_1g_3733)
+    to avoid clashing with the extern ddr_fsp0_cfg[] declared in
+    cargt_lpddr4x_timing_shared.h.
+  - The PHY PIE has exactly 559 entries for all currently supported variants.
+  - The PIE inc file must NOT contain the closing "};" line of the array.
+
+
+Expected Array Sizes (from DDR Tool v4.0.0_8.8-, PHY FW2022.01)
+-----------------------------------------------------------------
+  Array               Entries   Notes
+  ------------------  -------   ------------------------------------------
+  ddr_ddrc_cfg        19        All current variants
+  ddr_ddrphy_cfg      131       All current variants
+  ddr_fsp0_cfg        33        All current variants
+  ddr_fsp1_cfg        34        All current variants
+  ddr_fsp2_cfg        34        All current variants
+  ddr_fsp0_2d_cfg     34        All current variants
+  ddr_phy_pie         559       All current variants
+  ddr_dram_fsp_cfg    3 blocks  One per FSP (P0/P1/P2)
+  trained_csr         88        From cargt_lpddr4x_{3200,3733}mts_csr.h
+
+
+ODT / MR11 Reference
+--------------------
+MR11 controls on-die termination and differs by rank topology:
+
+  Rank1 variants (512MB, 1GB):   MR11 = 0x46  in ddr_dram_fsp_cfg
+  Rank2 variants (2GB rank2):    MR11 = 0x26  in ddr_dram_fsp_cfg
+
+Using a rank2 part with rank1 timing (or vice versa) will produce marginal
+or failed DDR operation due to mismatched ODT impedance and PHY training
+parameters.  Always test each variant with the matching physical die.
+
+
+Adding a New Timing Variant
+---------------------------
+1. Run the NXP DDR Tool against the target part to produce a generated .c file.
+   Place it in generated_timings_for_reference/.
+
+2. Use the Python extraction pattern (see scripts or prior art in this session)
+   to split the generated file into inc files under include/:
+     ddrc_cfg, ddrphy_cfg, dram_fsp_cfg, fsp0_cfg, fsp1_cfg, fsp2_cfg,
+     fsp0_2d_cfg, phy_pie
+
+3. Verify each inc file against the generated reference (diff on normalised
+   {0x...} lines).  Pay particular attention to ddrphy_cfg — a single wrong
+   register value (e.g. 0x20008) will cause silent DDR training failure.
+
+4. Create cargt_lpddr4x_<size>_<speed>mts_timing.c following the structure
+   described above.  Use variant-specific names for all static arrays.
+
+5. Add an extern declaration and a case to select_dram_timing() in spl-cargt.c.
+
+6. If rank2: verify that the DDRC addr map registers (0x4e300080/84, 0x4e300110)
+   are set for dual-rank, and that the rank-2 patch in spl-cargt.c covers the
+   new variant if needed.
+
+7. Rebuild and test with the matching physical part.  Do not validate rank1
+   timing with rank2 hardware or vice versa.
